Fishery Culturing fishes in fresh water ponds & estuarine water, catching fish 
from fresh water streams, lakes, rivers & sea water, including preservation, 
transportation & marketing of fishes.

Net filtration pressure (NFP) Net pressure that promotes fluid outflow at the 
arterial end of a capillary, and fluid inflow at the venous end of a capillary; 
net pressure that promotes glomerular filtration in the kidneys.

Progesterone Hormone secreted by the corpus luteum and the placenta; 
prepares the uterus for pregnancy & inhibits the growth and ovulation of 
new follicles.

Protocooperation A mutually beneficial interaction between organisms in which 
the interaction is not physiologically necessary to the survival of either; 
non-obligatory mutualism.

Sleep A state of partial unconsciouness from which a person can be• aroused; 
associated with a. low level of activity in the reticular activating system. 
